# persist.snapshot -- the /usr/-callable dump-only surface
# (persist_helper->trigger_dump) and its capability posture: default
# deny, operator grant/revoke through the capability verb, and the
# property that distinguishes it from the dump-and-exit path -- the
# runtime keeps serving after the dump. Verbs that run after the
# trigger_dump call execute in later tasks over the same telnet
# session, so each one is evidence the server survived the snapshot.
#
# Runs against a base boot; no example deploy, no module:
#   DGD_BIN=<dgd> scripts/drive-verbs-smoke.sh scripts/verbsets/persist-dump.verbset
# The snapshot-file landing itself is asserted by
# scripts/persist-dump-smoke.sh, which boots, drives this verbset, and
# checks state/snapshot while the driver is still up (the dump file
# lives outside the LPC root, so no verb can see it; and the kernel
# driver dumps on SIGTERM, so only a mid-run check discriminates).

# default-deny: no principal holds persist.snapshot at boot. The
# code-verb caller's principal is the console owner's user name.
cmd: code "/usr/System/sys/persist_helper"->trigger_dump()
expect: Error: capability denied: principal admin lacks persist.snapshot

# the operator grant path: a store entry through the KERNEL()-gated
# console verb
cmd: capability grant persist.snapshot admin
expect: capability: granted persist.snapshot to admin

# the choke-point every authority decision routes through answers true
cmd: code "/kernel/sys/capabilityd"->is_allowed("persist.snapshot", "admin")
expect: \$\d+ = 1

# the dump-only call now succeeds and returns immediately: the kfun
# marks the state for dumping, the driver writes the snapshot after
# this task completes
cmd: code "/usr/System/sys/persist_helper"->trigger_dump()
expect: \$\d+ = nil

# the runtime keeps serving after the dump: the same session still
# answers, and evaluation still works
cmd: status
expect: Server:\s+DGD
expect: Uptime:

cmd: code 2 + 3
expect: \$\d+ = 5

# capabilityd's own mutators stay KERNEL()-gated: a console code caller
# is refused (the operator path above is the only console route)
cmd: code "/kernel/sys/capabilityd"->grant("persist.snapshot", "evil")
expect: Error: capabilityd: grant not callable from outside /kernel

# revoke, and the surface denies again -- the operator lever is real
cmd: capability revoke persist.snapshot admin
expect: capability: revoked persist.snapshot from admin

cmd: code "/kernel/sys/capabilityd"->is_allowed("persist.snapshot", "admin")
expect: \$\d+ = 0

cmd: code "/usr/System/sys/persist_helper"->trigger_dump()
expect: Error: capability denied: principal admin lacks persist.snapshot
